Full Disk (FDE/SED)	Laptops, physical drive theft.	Physical theft of the storage device.	No protection once the OS is running.
Volume/Partition	Flexible OS-level protection for desktops and servers.	Physical theft; offers configurable security.	Software-dependent; may not hide metadata.
File/Folder	Granular security on file servers and multi-user systems.	Unauthorized access by other users/malware on the same system.	Complex management; potential for user error and data loss.
In practice, a defense-in-depth approach is often used: FDE/Volume Encryption to protect the device if stolen, and File Encryption for the most sensitive documents to protect them from other users and software-based attacks.

